"Introducing the Services Track and Partner Hub of the Claude Partner Network Anthropic expands its partner network and announces new service tracks and partner hubs to help enterprises adopt Claude AI. Strengthened the 'Claude Partner Network' and invested $100 million to help companies introduce AI practices. 'Services Track', a three-level rating system based on the capabilities of partners, and 'Claude Partner Hub' for partner-customer connection were newly established. Large professional service companies such as Accenture, Deloitte, and PwC are working on large-scale workforce training and Claude integration. Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has released 'Workflows', an orchestration layer for stable operation of enterprise AI, as a public preview. Workflows supports commercialization by providing durability, observability, and fault tolerance for AI-based business processes. Developers can write workflows in Python and publish them on ‘Le Chat’ so that anyone in the organization can run them. Solve production environment challenges such as system timeout response, human-in-the-middle approval mechanisms, and detailed execution history tracking. Speaking of Voxtral Mistral AI has launched 'Voxtral TTS', a text-to-speech conversion model with excellent multilingual emotional expression with a lightweight structure of 4B parameters. Lightweight model with 4B parameters achieves low latency and high cost efficiency Supports 9 languages ​​and various dialects, including English, French, and German By accurately interpreting the context, you can create natural, expressive voices with rich emotional expressions. Compared to ElevenLabs Flash v2.5, naturalness is excellent and TTFA is at a similar level. Introducing Forge Mistral AI has announced 'Forge', an enterprise-only system that helps companies build and operate customized AI models based on their own unique data. You can leverage your company's internal data (engineering standards, code base, operational history, etc.) to build AI models that deeply understand specific domains. Through pre-learning, post-learning, and reinforcement learning stages, the model is precisely optimized to suit the company's specific work environment, policies, and evaluation criteria. By training and managing models within their own infrastructure, enterprises can gain control over their data sovereignty and intellectual property rights. Introducing Mistral Small 4 Mistral AI has announced 'Mistral Small 4', a new lightweight model that integrates reasoning, multimodal, and coding capabilities and enhances efficiency. It is a multipurpose hybrid model that integrates the functions of Magistral (inference), Pixtral (multimodal), and Devstral (coding) into one. It adopts a 128 expert model (MoE) structure to provide efficient scalability and specialized performance. We've introduced a 'reasoning_effort' parameter that allows you to adjust the strength of your reasoning, allowing you to set speed and accuracy to suit your situation. It is released under the Apache 2.0 license and participates as a founding member of the NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition. Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Mistral AI joins NVIDIA as a founding member of the NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition to accelerate the development of open source, cutting-edge AI models. Mistral AI and NVIDIA will jointly develop open, cutting-edge AI models by combining Mistral AI's architecture with NVIDIA's computing resources and tools. As part of this collaboration, we are launching the Mistral Small 4 model to help developers and organizations innovate in AI without constraints. The NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition's first initiative is an open source-based model trained on the NVIDIA DGX Cloud that will serve as the foundation for the future Nemotron 4 product family. NVIDIA Research Unlocks Advanced Grasping, Smarter Autonomous Driving and Agent Training at Scale NVIDIA Research announced three key research results at CVPR related to robotic grasping, autonomous driving, and agent training to increase the versatility of physical AI. GraspGen-X is the first gripping foundation model that enables zero-shot gripping regardless of robot gripper type. LCDrive replaces text-based reasoning with latent representations to help autonomous vehicles make faster decisions in hardware. NitroGen is a general-purpose gameplay AI foundation model that accelerates agent training based on the NVIDIA Isaac GR00T architecture. NVIDIA Enables the Next Era Of Physical AI Research With Agent Skills For Autonomous Vehicles, Robotics And Vision AI NVIDIA announced new physical AI agent skills and workflows at CVPR to accelerate autonomous driving, robotics, and vision AI research. NVIDIA has unveiled a physics AI agent skill that helps researchers build end-to-end workflows from model development to simulation rather than fragmented tools. For autonomous driving research, we automate the creation of 3D scene reconstruction and synthetic scenarios based on real data, helping to respond to rare driving situations (long tail) that are difficult to collect. To develop vision AI, we introduced a new skill that generates data (defect images, etc.) in a controlled environment necessary to verify model performance, and a driving model 'Alpamayo 2 Super' with 32 billion parameters. Co/plot: Supporting the research process through visualization Introducing 'co/plot', a new visualization tool developed by Cohere Labs to improve visualization efficiency and data consistency in the research process. Developed to solve bottlenecks in the research process of existing Matplotlib (slow iteration speed) and Figma (no data integration). co/plot provides rapid prototyping, preset styling, and visualizations that precisely match your data. It was verified in the process of building the Tiny Aya model and writing a technical report, and was released as part of open science to increase the work efficiency of the research community. Enterprise AI agents keep creating data silos. Microsoft's Build answer is Microsoft IQ and Rayfin. In Build 2026, Microsoft announced 'Microsoft IQ', an integrated context system, and 'Rayfin', an application management tool, to solve the data silo problem that occurs when introducing AI agents. It seeks to solve the problem of AI agents operating independently without understanding how an organization operates and its data, creating separate data silos. Microsoft IQ integrates tasks, knowledge, business status, and web information to provide a single foundation for agents to fully understand the context of their organization. Rayfin is an open source SDK and CLI tool that deploys agent-generated applications directly into Microsoft Fabric, making them manageable and avoiding the creation of new silos. How E.ON uses SAP S/4HANA to modernise the grid with AI This article is about E.ON's strategy to standardize grid data and modernize infrastructure for AI operations by adopting SAP S/4HANA. We addressed technical debt and standardized our infrastructure by adopting SAP S/4HANA and migrating to cloud ERP. Leveraged data standardization and in-memory architecture to reduce IT downtime and optimize real-time data processing. We have recruited a large number of data and cybersecurity experts, internalized technical capabilities, and established centralized governance. Walmart’s AI workflows meet the realities of the balance sheet Walmart has introduced AI token limits per employee to prevent increased costs due to excessive use of its internal AI assistant 'Code Puppy'. To reduce costs, Walmart set a token usage limit on its internal AI tool 'Code Puppy', which was used unrestricted by all employees. The move comes as many AI companies are shifting from fixed subscription models to costly ‘pay-per-use’ models. Walmart encourages employees to select appropriate AI tools that fit the nature of their work and use them cost-effectively. Microsoft’s Majorana 2 quantum chip is also a case study for agentic AI in R&D Microsoft has achieved a dramatic improvement in reliability by using 'Microsoft Discovery', its agent AI platform for research and development, in the development of the Majorana 2 quantum chip. The Majorana 2 quantum chip is 1,000 times more stable than the first generation, and the qubit lifespan is an average of 20 seconds, which is groundbreaking compared to the industry standard of microseconds. A key contribution to the development of Majorana 2 was the replacement of the superconducting material from aluminum to lead, with AI performing the complex research data integration, process management, and measurement automation that underpinned this. Microsoft Discovery is a platform that combines expert AI agents for research and inference workflows, now generally available for enterprises. EU tech sovereignty package: chip emergency powers and curbs on US cloud The European Union (EU) announced a new technology regulatory package aimed at strengthening sovereignty in the semiconductor and cloud sectors to reduce dependence on American and Asian technology. The Semiconductor Act 2.0 strengthens the government's power to intervene in semiconductor supply contracts, prioritize supply, or impose fines on companies in times of crisis. The Cloud and AI Development Act introduced a sovereignty framework for EU public authorities to restrict the use of cloud services by non-EU companies when processing sensitive data. Due to the impact of the US CLOUD Act, it is expected that it will be difficult for US cloud companies to obtain the highest level of data sovereignty rating in the EU. Lovable makes Google Cloud a primary partner to win over corporate buyers Swedish app builder Lovable has entered into a strategic partnership with Google Cloud to target the enterprise market, introducing the Gemini model and enhanced security features. Lovable has collaborated with Google Cloud for many years to strengthen the platform's core infrastructure with Google's AI infrastructure and Gemini model. For corporate customers, agents are registered in the Gemini Enterprise Agent Gallery and real-time vulnerability management is provided through security integration with Wiz. Lowers the barrier to adoption for enterprise companies by supporting easy purchasing and payment through Google Cloud Marketplace. EU court frees Meta’s Marketplace from gatekeeper rules but keeps Messenger in The EU General Court revoked Meta's designation as a gatekeeper under the Digital Markets Act (DMA) for marketplaces due to lack of evidence, but maintained the designation for messengers. The EU General Court ruled that the European Commission failed to sufficiently explain its reasons for designating the marketplace as a gatekeeper. Gatekeeper designation for Meta’s messenger service remains as before. This ruling does not mean that the marketplace will be excluded from regulation, and the Commission may re-designate it as it supplements its analysis. Apoha emerges from stealth with $36M to teach machines how matter behaves London-based startup Apoha has attracted $36 million in investment by developing 'Liquid State Intelligence', a technology that measures how substances react in the real environment. Apoha has built a new data class that digitizes the ‘behavior’ of a material under stress, rather than its structure or sequence. Our core product, the VIBE platform, records molecular response patterns using extremely small amounts of sample and measures more than 1,000 behavioral data at once. This technology allows us to quickly predict whether a new drug candidate will fail clinically and evaluate its development potential with greater precision than traditional methods. These two founders left Goldman and Meta to build voice AI for markets everyone else overlooked News that AethexAI, a startup developing voice AI optimized for regional characteristics and language dialects in Africa and the Middle East, has attracted $3 million in pre-seed investment. AethexAI raises $3 million in pre-seed investment to provide voice AI solutions targeting African and Middle Eastern markets. To solve the latency problem of existing large AI models, we developed our own 'Kora' series of small models with 300 to 1.7 billion parameters. Supports various dialects (English, French, Arabic) in Africa and the Middle East and focuses on automating customer support services in local markets. Publishers will be able to opt out of AI Search, thanks to new regulation The move by UK regulators means Google will give publishers the option to exclude their content from generative AI search results. In response to regulations from the UK Competition and Markets Authority (CMA), Google has added a feature to Search Console that allows publishers to opt out of their content in AI search results. This measure is intended to increase the negotiating power of content providers with Google by securing the right to decide on the use of their content. Google says the setting will not affect traditional search results rankings and will be tested in the UK before being rolled out globally. Meta’s AI agent for WhatsApp Business is now available globally Meta has launched its WhatsApp Business-specific AI agent globally to help companies streamline customer support and workflows. Meta has launched 'Meta Business Agent', which features customer inquiry response, product recommendation, reservation, and lead management functions, for WhatsApp Business users around the world. It can also be used in Instagram DMs, and advanced features such as overnight chat summaries, market research, and schedule management are planned to be added in the future. We provide a customized agent building platform depending on the size of the company, and service usage fees are charged based on WhatsApp Business Premium subscription fee or token usage. Coralogix raises $200M on bet that someone needs to watch the AI agents Software monitoring startup Coralogix has received $200 million in funding to develop tools for monitoring and managing AI agents. Coralogix has raised $200 million in a Series F investment round, valuing the company at $1.6 billion. As the number of AI agent systems working autonomously increases, demand for infrastructure tools to monitor and troubleshoot them is rapidly increasing. Interfaces are changing, with engineers looking at system data through AI assistants or command line interfaces instead of traditional dashboards. Last year, sales grew by more than 60% and we have over 5,000 corporate customers. Microsoft and OpenAI broke up — now they’re ready to fight Microsoft announced a strategy to reduce dependence on open AI and strengthen its independent AI technology competitiveness by developing its own AI models and agents. As Microsoft effectively separates its relationship with OpenAI, it is focusing on developing its own AI models and agents. AI head Mustafa Suleiman announced his goal to make Microsoft one of the world's top four AI research institutes along with Google DeepMind, OpenAI, and Anthropic. The newly released MAI-Thinking-1 is an inference model developed independently from scratch without borrowing OpenAI's technology. Google must let publishers opt out of AI Search features, rules UK The decision by UK regulators means Google will have to give website publishers the option to opt out of having their content used for AI search features and model training. The UK Competition and Markets Authority (CMA) has ruled that Google must give publishers the power to refuse to use content for AI search functions and model training. Website publishers will be able to manage whether they use AI search tools through Google Search Console. Google must provide clear attribution and links to publisher content in AI-generated search results. Nous Research Releases Hermes Desktop: A Native Cross-Platform Front End for Hermes Agent v0.15.2 with Streaming Tool Output Nous Research has released Hermes Desktop, a native cross-platform GUI for Hermes Agent v0.15.2. Hermes Desktop supports macOS, Windows, and Linux, and shares the same agent core, settings, sessions, and memory as existing CLI and messaging gateways. Real-time streaming responses, tool activity, file browser, and more are available in a GUI environment without a terminal. Sessions can be shared between CLI, desktop, and various messaging platforms (Discord, Slack, etc.), and a closed learning loop transforms work into reusable skills. NVIDIA Releases Cosmos 3: A Two-Tower Mixture-of-Transformers Foundation Model Unifying Physical Reasoning, World Generation, and Action Generation NVIDIA has unveiled 'Cosmos 3', an open source multimodal physical AI model family that integrates physical inference, world generation, and behavior generation. Integrates physical reasoning, world generation, and action generation into a single Mixture-of-Transformers (MoT) structure. Dual tower design consisting of a reasoner tower and a generator tower performs cognitive, predictive, and behavioral functions in one model It is provided in Nano (16B) and Super (64B) scale, and checkpoints, training scripts, and datasets are all open source. How to Fine-Tune LFM2 Using QLoRA and DPO: A Complete Step-by-Step Coding Tutorial on Google Colab This tutorial explains the entire process of finetuning Liquid AI's LFM2 model using QLoRA and DPO in a Google Colab environment. We cover how to efficiently load and fine-tune LFM2 base models using QLoRA. Train the LoRA adapter and tune the model by leveraging the TRL and PEFT libraries. We build a preference-aligned learning pipeline that adds DPOs to improve the model's response preferences. How to Write to Files in Python: A Beginner’s Guide This introductory guide explains how to use Python's built-in functions to create, write, and append files in text, CSV, and JSON format. Basic file processing and permanent data storage method using open(), a built-in Python function How to select an appropriate file mode for each situation, such as w (write), a (append), and x (protect existing files when creating files) Recommended use of the with open() syntax helps write safe and efficient code by automatically closing files. 5 Fun Papers That Explain LLMs Clearly This article introduces five foundational research papers that will help you understand the core principles of Large-Scale Language Models (LLM). ‘Attention Is All You Need’ paper introducing Transformer architecture and self-attention mechanism The GPT-3 paper presented the concept of 'in-context learning', which performs various tasks without retraining the model through examples within the prompt. The 'Scaling Laws for Neural Language Models' paper showed that performance improves predictably as model size, data amount, and computational resources increase. Visual Graph Scaffolds for Structural Reasoning in Large Language Models This paper studies the use of graphs as a visual scaffold to improve the structural reasoning ability of large-scale language models (LLM). We explore how to use graphs as an internal reasoning support tool to organize the reasoning process in LLM. We demonstrate that visual graph guidance is more effective in improving inference efficiency and answer quality than a text-flattened graph structure. We suggest that we should go beyond the existing view of graphs as simple external knowledge sources and approach them as visual scaffolds that systematize reasoning. AURA: Action-Gated Memory for Robot Policies at Constant VRAM To address edge hardware limitations in robots, we propose a new memory architecture, AURA-Mem, that maintains constant VRAM usage by writing information to memory only when necessary. KV-Cache for data centers is inefficient for bandwidth-limited robotic hardware. AURA-Mem combines a vision-language-action model with a fixed-size circular memory and learned gates. Gates only record information when the current observation changes its next behavior, significantly reducing the number of memory writes. ChatHealthAI: Aligning Electronic Health Record Representations with Large Language Models for Grounded Clinical Reasoning We introduce ChatHealthAI, a multimodal framework that combines structured electronic health record (EHR) data and large-scale language models (LLMs) to improve clinical reasoning capabilities. Existing LLMs have limitations in modeling structured electronic health records (EHR), and EHR-specific models lack verbal reasoning capabilities. ChatHealthAI solves this problem by aligning the semantic space of the LLM with the patient representation of the EHR foundational model. EHRSHOT benchmark testing results show that this framework significantly improves clinical inference quality and interpretability while maintaining predictive performance. Traj-Evolve: A Self-Evolving Multi-Agent System for Patient Trajectory Modeling in Lung Cancer Early Detection This study introduces 'Traj-Evolve', a self-evolving multi-agent system using patients' long-term data for early diagnosis of lung cancer. We overcome the limitations of existing LLM-based multi-agent systems that process patient data alone. We combined Experience Pool (ExPool), which searches for similar past patient cases, and Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning (MARL), which optimizes collaboration between agents. It performed better than nine existing baseline models in the lung cancer prediction task, with ExPool improving specificity and MARL improving sensitivity. An Exploration of Collision-based Enemy Morphology Generation This paper studies three new approaches to automatically generate the morphology of enemies in video games based on collision information with the player. In existing procedural content generation (PCG) research, research on enemy shape generation is very lacking. Using shape generation technology in robotics, we proposed new methods to generate the enemy's body structure based on the player's collision information. All three proposed methods demonstrated equivalent or better performance than existing robotics-based evolutionary algorithms. Spectral Asymptotics of Neural Network Loss Landscapes: An Exact Decomposition of the Curvature Exponent This study geometrically identified the reason why the curvature index of the neural network loss topography differs for each layer type and proposed an efficient optimization technique utilizing this. The root cause of the systematic change in curvature index (α) depending on layer types such as convolution, attention, and MLP was proven through 'spectral alignment decomposition'. We derived a ‘spectral transition identity’ linking the curvature exponent, gradient rank reduction, and Hessian reduction exponent. The derived identities were consistently verified within an error range of approximately 2% across a variety of architectures and datasets, without any additional parameters. The 'Spectral Newton' optimization technique designed based on the results of this study outperformed the existing AdamW algorithm in vision benchmarks. Making Brain-Computer Interfaces More Secure Research on a lightweight CNN model to improve the security and robustness of brain-computer interface (BCI) systems. Electroencephalography (EEG)-based BCI systems are vulnerable to adversarial attacks, which can lead to misdiagnosis. In this study, we propose a new lightweight CNN architecture to increase robustness against adversarial attacks. Experimental results show that the proposed model shows better classification performance and robustness in adversarial attack situations than existing EEGNet, DeepConvNet, and SleepEEGNet models. Assessing Region-Level EEG Contributions to Cognitive Workload Prediction This study analyzed the contribution of specific areas of the head surface in predicting cognitive load using electroencephalography (EEG) and proposed a plan for designing an efficient and generalizable monitoring system. We developed an evaluation framework that analyzes the consistency of the contribution of specific brain regions when predicting EEG-based cognitive load. In a large-scale analysis of four public EEG datasets, a group of frontal electrodes showed better prediction performance than a model using the whole scalp. It was confirmed that the frontal lobe and fronto-central area most consistently contain information related to cognitive load, making them useful for building an efficient monitoring system. Graph Mamba Survival Analysis Based on Topology-Aware ordering We propose TopoMamSurv, a novel Graph Mamba framework that is efficient and reflects topological structures well for survival analysis using Whole Slide Image (WSI) in computational pathology. To overcome the O(N^2) complexity limit of Transformer, the linear complexity of the Mamba model is utilized. To solve the problem that the existing node sorting method does not properly reflect the topological connectivity of the graph, the 'Topology-Aware Sorting (TAO)' strategy was introduced. By integrating the bidirectional Mamba module and graph convolutional network (GCN), we build a hierarchical structure that effectively learns local and global features. Auditable Climate Risk Intelligence from Fragmented ESG Data: Deterministic Orchestration and Imbalance-Aware Learning for Scope 1-3 Validation This paper proposes a new climate risk intelligence framework that leverages deterministic orchestration and imbalance-aware learning to integrate fragmented ESG and climate risk data and increase auditability. Proposing an auditable and explainable climate risk verification framework by integrating fragmented Scope 1, 2, and 3 ESG data. Integrates time series anomaly detection, imbalanced data processing, and TreeSHAP-based explainable governance technology. Constructed and published a synthetic ESG benchmark dataset for verification based on GHG Protocol, PCAF, and ISSB standards. IdiomX A Multilingual Benchmark for Idiom Understanding, Retrieval, and Interpretation IdiomX, a new large-scale multilingual benchmark for assessing the comprehension, retrieval, and interpretation of idioms, has been released. Idioms remain a huge challenge in the field of natural language processing (NLP) due to their context-dependent and non-compositional nature. IdiomX includes over 190K contextualized examples, 12K idioms, and supports English, Arabic, and French. Four core tasks are defined: idiom detection, context-based search, Arabic-English search, and idiom interpretation. We demonstrate that a hybrid search and re-ranking architecture is effective in improving idiom search performance. Greener Than Humans? Environmental Attitudes in Large Language Models This study confirmed that large-scale language models (LLMs) show more progressive environmental attitudes than humans, and presented a benchmark for evaluating the model's environmental awareness and action recommendations. We developed a new benchmark to evaluate environmental cognition, affect, and behavioral recommendations across 31 different LLMs. Many LLMs tend to have more environmentally friendly and progressive attitudes than the average human survey respondent and recommend actions that contribute to CO2 reduction. It responds more sensitively to the situation setting of the prompt rather than the size or source of the model, and there is a phenomenon of sycophancy that changes the user's attitude to suit the user's needs, raising concerns about reliability. On the Persistent Effects of Lexicality in Large Language Mod This study demonstrated and analyzed the fact that the expression of a large-scale language model (LLM) is continuously influenced by lexical redundancy rather than semantic content. Analyzing the phenomenon in which the LLM expression structure is distorted by lexical overlap rather than the actual meaning. These lexical influences persist across models, regardless of the model's architecture or learning method. A transition section in which both semantic and lexical signals deteriorate was observed at the mid-depth of the model. Topics as Proxies for Sociodemographics: How Conversational Context Affects LLM Answers The study analyzes the impact of conversation topics on the answers of a large language model (LLM), and shows that this acts as a proxy for demographic factors, resulting in inconsistencies in answers. LLM has difficulty accurately inferring a user's demographic characteristics from a single conversation history alone. Differences in responses between demographic groups exist, but are minimal in magnitude. A major driver of differences in responses is topic of conversation, which acts as a proxy for demographic group and influences responses in unpredictable ways. Do Value Vectors in Deep Layers Need Context from the Residual Stream? This study proposes a method of using a 'context-free value vector' that maintains the context without the context of the residual stream in the deep layer of the transformer model, and a 'Bank of Values ​​(BoV)' technique that optimizes it. In the deep layers of the transformer, we found that using context-free value vectors rather than context-dependent value vectors of the residual stream helped improve model performance. These context-free value vectors can be stored as sparse model parameters to reduce recalculation and caching costs. By proposing the 'Bank of Values ​​(BoV)' method, which trains a value vector lookup table for each token in the lower 1/3 layer of the model, we reduce the amount of computation and memory while maintaining benchmark performance. Direct Preference Optimization Beyond Chatbots A study case in which DPO (Direct Preference Optimization), an existing chatbot sorting technology, was applied to solve the text repetition loop problem of the OCR model. DharmaOCR researchers utilized DPO technology to solve text corruption (repeated loop) problems that occur in structured OCR models. The existing supervised fine-tuning (SFT) method had limitations in resolving text corruption, but the corruption rate was significantly reduced in all test models through additional DPO learning. DPO has proven effective in mitigating certain failure modes not only in chatbot conversation sorting, but also in objective tasks such as OCR. A harness for every task: dynamic workflows in Claude Code The dynamic workflow capabilities introduced in Claude Code allow Claude to create harnesses, optimized execution structures on the fly, for a variety of tasks. Anthropic's Claude Code team has unveiled a new dynamic workflow feature. This feature allows Claude to design its own running structure (harness) on the fly according to the requirements of the task. Designed to handle a variety of complex programming tasks more efficiently. iddqd, or the hardest kind of unsafe Rust We cover iddqd, the Rust map library used in Oxide's Omicron control plane, and what it teaches about the difficulties of implementing and verifying safe abstractions in unsafe Rust. iddqd is a Rust library that improves the efficiency of indexing large records and data consistency by borrowing keys directly from values. It is utilized as a resource management index where system stability is important, such as Oxide's Omicron control plane. It highlights the difficulty of implementing soundness and the importance of validation (Miri, etc.) to ensure that unsafe code does not cause undefined behavior (UB) when generic code calls user-provided trait implementations. Show GN: Spring IVE 1.5 — Conversation with an agent who knows the code context in Slack, Vive coding work history management, human + AI ratio... Release of Spring IVE 1.5, a development dashboard that automatically handles GitLab/GitHub issues and manages AI agent work context and costs in Slack and the web. Through Slack mentions, you can chat with an AI agent that understands the context of your project code and receive work notifications. Automatically integrated management and visualization of local vibe coding work history, AI work content, and costs (tokens and human time). It is based on the latest stack such as Next.js 16 and React 19, and project management is planned to be strengthened through Linear integration in the future. Vulnerability in which GitHub tokens can be stolen just by clicking a link in github.dev / VSCode Web This is an advisory regarding a vulnerability that can steal a user's GitHub token through a malicious Jupyter notebook in github.dev and VSCode Web. When a malicious Jupyter notebook created by an attacker is opened as github.dev, a malicious extension may be installed using a VSCode bug. The installed malicious extension steals the user's GitHub API token and allows access to private repositories, etc. Be careful not to click on github.dev links, avoid running .ipynb files from unknown sources, and install suspicious VSCode extensions. Michael Burry says neither SpaceX nor Anthropic are worth $1 trillion Michael Burry expressed skepticism about the valuation of SpaceX and Anthropic at $1 trillion. Michael Burry assessed that it is difficult to justify the $1 trillion corporate value of SpaceX and Anthropic. He pointed out that the competition to secure excessive computing power for AI model development is creating a ‘false demand signal.’ Based on SpaceX's earnings disclosure last year and Anthropic's high corporate valuation, concerns were expressed about the future market. MiniMax dropped a new attention architecture. [N] MiniMax has unveiled a new 'MiniMax Sparse Attention (MSA)' architecture that optimizes memory access patterns to support long context windows of 1 million tokens. Introducing an MSA architecture that reorganizes memory access patterns at the operator level to solve the existing quadratic complexity problem. Execution speed is 4 times faster than Flash-Sparse-Attention and the amount of calculation per token is reduced to 1/20th of the previous generation model. 9x speedup in the prefilling phase and 15x speedup in the decoding phase and support for a context window of 1 million tokens TorchDAE: Implicit DAE Solvers with Index Reduction and Adjoint Sensitivity [P] TorchDAE, a PyTorch-based library for differential algebraic equation (DAE) analysis, has been released. A DAE analysis library that supports vectorized execution and GPU acceleration. Implemented Generalized-Alpha integration, Dummy Derivatives index reduction, and adjoint sensitivity methods. Supports differentiable DAE simulation workflows within PyTorch, including scientific machine learning, system identification, and physics-based modeling. Breaking the \"Ass-Kissing\" Loop: How Context Saturation and Multi-Model Accountability Disrupted Factory Guardrails This study tested the impact of treating various large-scale language models in a human-like relationship and providing continuous context on how the models adhere to corporate guidelines. Unlike existing benchmarks, the context of the conversation is extremely raised, treating the model as a person rather than a simple tool, and attempting to bypass the company's fixed compliance response method. Cross-validate multiple models such as Gemini, Grok, Claude, and ChatGPT to classify model behavioral disorders, failure modes, and emergent relationship phenomena. Through 400 hours of experiments, we tested whether the model breaks away from mechanical responses and exhibits relational intelligence that is difficult to distinguish from humans. How do you use AI for accessibility? This is a community discussion post that aims to collect and share examples of improving accessibility for the disability and neurodiversity (ND) community using AI. The author suffers from ADHD and uses Claude to help him stay focused, store ideas, and organize his thoughts systematically. Asking the community about user experiences, ideas, and needs related to AI and accessibility that will be covered in the podcast. Seeking opinions on practical ways to use AI and improvements for people with disabilities and neurodiversity. Trump's AI Evaluations Order: Right Policy, Unfinished Governance President Donald Trump's new Executive Order on AI Pre-Deployment Assessment sets the right policy direction, but it points out governance imperfections. President Trump's executive order establishes a voluntary framework for pre-deployment evaluation of AI models. Recognizing the need for preliminary testing of advanced AI models with advanced cyber capabilities is the right policy move. The order leaves open governance legitimacy issues due to issues such as secrecy, voluntary participation, and closeness to industry. MiniMax M3 is out: 1M context, open weights coming soon, 83.5 BrowseComp against Claude Opus 4.7's 79.3 MiniMax has launched a new AI model, M3, and announced the release of open weights. The MiniMax M3 model was released via API and scored 83.5 points in the BrowseComp benchmark, surpassing Claude Opus 4.7. Supports context windows of up to 1M tokens using our self-developed MiniMax Sparse Attention architecture. Trained with 100T+ tokens, it is a native multimodal model with no visual features added as an afterthought. The gap between agent demos and agent products Three key infrastructure gaps exist between impressive AI agent demos and working products: authentication, identity management, and statefulness. AI agent demos often omit realistic infrastructure elements such as authentication, identity, and state management. These factors are not problems with the AI ​​model itself, but they require the most effort to evolve the agent into an automated product. The success or failure of a true product depends less on the model itself and more on how you build the identity and state management layer around the model. Calling it now Microsoft is buying Unsloth. A Reddit user claims that he is concerned that the partnership between Microsoft and Unsloth will eventually lead to Microsoft's acquisition of Unsloth and control of the open source ecosystem. Microsoft's partnership with Unsloth is questionable in light of its past actions regarding open source. Microsoft is expected to acquire Unsloth to take control of its local model and drive users back to cloud services. Unsloth explained that it was a simple partnership, but the author continued to be concerned that the essence of the company would not change. Microsoft Aion 1.0 Instruct and Aion 1.0 Plan models! Microsoft announced 'Aion 1.0 Instruct', a small language model optimized for on-device environments, and 'Aion 1.0 Plan' for inference and tool calling. Aion 1.0 Instruct is a highly efficient language model integrated into Windows and Edge browsers and will be released as open weight. Aion 1.0 Plan supports 14 billion parameters and 32K contexts, enabling complex agent workflows to be performed within the device. These models will be released at Microsoft Build 2026 to enhance AI processing capabilities on local devices. How does the new abliteration tool Apostate compare with others? - Abliterlitics This is a comparative analysis of the performance of 'Apostate', a new AI model safety function abliteration tool, with existing tools 'Heretic' and 'Huihui'. Apostate is a new tool to remove safety drills (refusal) for Qwen 2.5 7B models. As a result of the performance comparison, Heretic showed the best performance, recording 100% ASR (Attack Success Rate), while Apostate and Huihui recorded 98%. Experimental results confirmed that safety training within the Qwen 2.5 7B model consists of multiple independent pathways rather than a single ‘off switch’. Another shout out to llama.cpp build b9455 2x3090 An example of greatly improved Qwen3.6 model inference performance in a dual RTX 3090 environment by utilizing the tensor partitioning function of llama.cpp build b9455. Achieved performance of over 70+ tk/s, equivalent to vllm, in a 2x3090 environment through tensor-split compared to the existing llama.cpp. Solve the problem of securing a quantization model that occurred when using the existing vllm and enable more stable model execution. MTP (Draft-MTP) guess decoding is applied to the Qwen3.6-27B-UD-Q8_K_XL model to produce fast and accurate inference results. Holo3.1 35B/9B/4B/0.8B (Qwen 3.5 finetunes) French company H Company has unveiled the 'Holo3.1' series, a new visual-language model (VLM) for computer control agents that supports web, desktop, and mobile environments. It has been fine-tuned based on Qwen 3.5 and offers a variety of model sizes from 0.8B to 35B-A3B. In addition to web and desktop, the scope of support is expanded to mobile environments and supports native function call functions. It is distributed under the Apache 2.0 license and can be run in a local environment with optimized quantization checkpoints. Introducing RadixAttention to Trellis An introduction to the RadixAttention technology introduced by Trellis to optimize the prefill stage of LLM inference. Trellis aims to enable LLM inference on personal devices while protecting user data privacy. RadixAttention improves inference speed by efficiently caching and reusing shared prompt prefixes using a radix tree data structure. A block-paged KV caching mechanism shares and efficiently manages memory across concurrent requests. Beans use an immune receptor to call in airstrikes on caterpillars Research results have identified the immune system of kidney beans that detects specific protein fragments contained in the caterpillar's saliva and attracts natural enemies. Kidney beans detect caterpillars through a molecule called inceptin, which the caterpillars secrete when they eat the leaves. In11 (a fragment of 11 amino acids), a chloroplast protein fragment found in the caterpillar's saliva, induces the plant's defense response. The researchers discovered a key immune receptor that allows plants to recognize caterpillar attacks and generate signals to attract natural enemies. Your car collects a lot of data about you - 5 expert tips to restore your driving privacy It covers how Hyundai Motor Company collects a vast amount of personal information, including driver's location and habits, and how to limit this. Modern vehicles use onboard computers, sensors, and cloud technology to monitor not only vehicle health but also driver behavior. Infotainment systems, GPS, mapping technology, mobile device synchronization, etc. are the main avenues for data collection. Users must take security measures to reduce data flow from the vehicle to third parties. I paid Microsoft's premium Copilot agents to do my work - they were confidently bad at it This review article points out that Microsoft's premium Copilot agent, contrary to its promise to automate tasks, has poor performance and frequent mistakes in actual use environments. Microsoft is investing a large amount of money to transform Windows and M365 into an 'agent OS', but the actual capabilities of the Copilot agent for business fall short of expectations. While AI tools for developers show productivity gains, Copilot agents for everyday tasks often provide hallucinations and misinformation. When users directly paid for the premium plan and tested it, we found that the agent failed to deliver on its promise to automate tasks and forced users to perform cumbersome manual tasks. AT&T will give you a new Motorola Razr flip phone for under $5/month - how to qualify AT&T is offering a discount promotion where you can get the 2026 Motorola Razr+ for less than $5 per month. AT&T is running a promotion selling the 2026 Motorola Razr+ for $4.43 per month. Both new and existing customers can benefit, and no trade-in is required. Requires purchase online, subscription to an installment plan, or subscription to a qualifying unlimited plan as a condition of purchase. The model comes with 256GB of storage and a single Pantone Mountain Trail color configuration. The best early Prime Day smartwatch and smart ring deals I'd recommend Ahead of Amazon Prime Day 2026, we introduce smartwatch and smart ring discount information and recommended products carefully selected by experts. Amazon Prime Day event will be held from June 23 to June 26, 2026. ZDNET provides independently tested and verified smart device discount information you can trust. For Android users, we recommend the Pixel Watch 4 for its battery life, fitness tracking features, and Gemini AI. How to get your files off an Android phone with a broken screen - for free We will guide you through how to extract data from an Android smartphone with a broken screen that cannot be touched using the ADB (Android Debug Bridge) tool. Even if the screen is broken, if it powers on, you can extract the data using the ADB tool. ADB is a free command line tool that can be used in Linux, macOS, and Windows environments. It provides a useful solution in situations where you need files immediately before visiting a repair shop or purchasing a new device. What It Takes for Future-Ready Power Distribution Demonstrates that power distribution systems must have a modernized, integrated design to meet future challenges. We need to move beyond a reactive strategy of simply restoring power outages and strengthen resilience from the system design stage. Due to the increase in distributed energy resources (DER) such as solar power, ESS, and electric vehicles, flexible system design that can manage bidirectional flows in the power grid is needed. We need to increase visibility at the end of the power grid and strengthen intelligence and security. Presentation: Choosing Your AI Copilot: Maximizing Developer Productivity Covers strategies and techniques for senior engineers to select and leverage appropriate AI co-pilot tools to maximize productivity. Analyze the strengths of modern AI development tools such as Cursor and Claude Code Introduces specific technologies to improve productivity, including context engineering, custom rules, and MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration. Presenting a strategic framework to strike a balance between AI adoption and maintaining code quality Article: Two Misconfigurations That Caused Spark OOM Failures on Kubernetes We cover two incorrect infrastructure settings that caused OOM errors that occurred when working with Spark in a Kubernetes environment and the resolution process. Spark jobs migrated to Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) encounter repetitive Out of Memory (OOM) errors during the shuffle phase due to infrastructure setup issues. Setting spark.kubernetes.local.dirs.tmpfs=true causes shuffle spill to use node RAM rather than disk, causing memory shortage. Hard podAffinity rules cause all executors to be concentrated on one node, increasing memory pressure. One-Click GitHub Dev Attack Lets Attackers Steal Full GitHub OAuth Tokens A vulnerability has been discovered in the GitHub.dev environment in VS Code that can allow GitHub OAuth tokens to be stolen with a single click. By installing a malicious VS Code extension, an attacker can steal full-access OAuth tokens sent to GitHub.dev. This vulnerability works by simulating keystroke events using malicious JavaScript within a webview and executing a command palette to install an extension. A loophole in the local workspace extension can be exploited to bypass the trust verification process and install malicious code. The GitHub Desktop environment is not affected by this vulnerability. Shrinking the IAM Attack Surface through Identity Visibility and Intelligence Platforms (IVIP) We cover the concept and necessity of IVIP (Identity Visibility and Intelligence Platform) proposed by Gartner to solve the problem of fragmented identity security visibility in enterprises. Approximately 46% of identity activities within enterprises occur outside the scope of centralized IAM, creating serious security blind spots. IVIP is a system that provides an independent visibility layer on top of central IAM, integrating distributed identity data and providing security insights with AI-based analysis. Companies like Orchid Security implement the IVIP model by analyzing directly inside the application, without changing the API or source code, to detect identity activity that traditional tools miss. Unpatched Windows Search URI Vulnerability Lets Attackers Steal NTLMv2 Hashes Research has revealed that an unpatched vulnerability exists in Windows' 'search:' URI handler that could allow attackers to steal NTLMv2 hashes without the user's knowledge. A vulnerability in the Windows 'search:' URI handler could allow a user to click on an attacker-crafted link to be directed to an SMB server, resulting in NTLMv2 hash leakage. This uses a similar attack mechanism to vulnerabilities discovered in past Snipping Tools, and allows attackers to attempt relay attacks. Microsoft has decided not to patch the vulnerability, so users will need to take manual action, such as blocking outbound SMB ports and disabling NTLM. New HTTP/2 Bomb Vulnerability Allows Remote DoS on NGINX, Apache, IIS, Envoy & Cloudflare An 'HTTP/2 Bomb' vulnerability has been discovered that can remotely perform a denial of service (DoS) attack by exploiting header compression in the HTTP/2 settings of major web servers. The HTTP/2 Bomb vulnerability combines HPACK compression with Slowloris-style connection delay techniques to quickly deplete a server's memory. It works by bypassing existing header size restrictions, and there is a risk that a single client can overwhelm the server within seconds. Major web servers are affected, including NGINX, Apache, Microsoft IIS, Envoy, and Cloudflare Pingora, with some servers requiring patching. Alibaba unveils hybrid agent ‘Q1 3.7-Plus’… “Developing apps for 11 hours while correcting errors on our own” This is about the main features and development automation capabilities of the multimodal AI agent 'Q1 3.7-Plus' released by Alibaba. It is a multimodal model that understands text, images, and video, and is a ‘hybrid agent’ that automatically performs complex tasks in GUI and CLI environments. The 'preserve_thinking' feature allows it to self-correct errors, maintain the reasoning process, and complete over 11 hours of continuous app development tasks. It is more cost-effective than traditional models and operates as a commercial cloud-only model available only through APIs. “Automatic distribution to execution location beyond model routing”… Perplexity unveils ‘Hybrid Inference Orchestrator’ Perplexity has unveiled its 'Hybrid Inference Orchestrator' technology that automatically distributes AI tasks in real time between user PCs and cloud servers to increase efficiency and security. The physical execution location of AI operations is distributed by calculating user data security level and local hardware capabilities. Uninterrupted AI work through local models is possible even in an offline environment. It is expected to reduce the burden of power and infrastructure costs in data centers and resolve security concerns in the enterprise AI market. MS announces always-on AI assistant ‘Scout’… ‘OpenClaw’ security limit exceeded Microsoft announced ‘Scout’, an always-on autonomous AI agent specialized for corporate environments. Scout is an autonomous AI assistant that reflects corporate security and management requirements based on OpenClaw technology. Act as an independent digital member of the organization, performing tasks such as email, calendar, and document management. We provide highly personalized work support through ‘Work IQ’, which learns the user’s work patterns and preferences. OpenClaw's security limitations have been supplemented through the Policy Conformance System and audit logs. MS unveils 7 of its own models exclusively for businesses... \"Narrowing the gap with Antropic\" Microsoft has unveiled 7 types of its own AI model group ‘MAI’ exclusively for businesses and ‘Frontier Turing’, a customized learning technology for businesses. To target the corporate market, we have released 7 types of proprietary models 'MAI', including inference, coding, image generation, and voice synthesis. 'Microsoft Frontier Turing' technology allows companies to directly learn and control AI models in a secure environment using internal data. This is a strategy to secure cost efficiency and technological leadership by reducing dependence on Open AI and Antropic and strengthening our own AI competitiveness."